{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline","id":806850,"title":"How to update the Septemi bloodline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T01:52:04-08:00","id":806850,"title":"How to update the Septemi bloodline?","content":"I honestly love the Septemi bloodline. But I have some problems on how to update the Abjurism Discipline or even if the Discipline sould be updated and instead chage into a merit or devotions? What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> I got a google doc up an running for the bloodline. I took some idea that were put in the forum and I thank everyone involved. So without further ado.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cvuaopl5laSlndKj4cgIl1j9q9PyMsGTYdnGNo4qvBc/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cvuaopl5laSlndKj4cgIl1j9q9PyMsGTYdnGNo4qvBc/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cvuaopl5laSlndKj4cgIl1j9q9PyMsGTYdnGNo4qvBc/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cvuaopl5laSlndKj4cgIl1j9q9PyMsGTYdnGNo4qvBc/edit?usp=docslist_api </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":".  File sharing. 02-25-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T02:53:44-08:00","id":806864,"title":"","content":"If you could update it to be an actual shield that is also physical too it could work as a discipline but you would have to seperate it from the others. Other than that it would be a Auspex/Dominate devotion my friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T02:59:54-08:00","id":806867,"title":"","content":"How would countering/destroying magical effects be dominate? But I love the idea of summoning a shield. Even if it runs counter to the subtle protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:13:31-08:00","id":806889,"title":"","content":"Not sure about the rest of it, but for their Bane, maybe they now possess a Virtue, but they don't gain Willpower from it; instead, whenever a night passes where they have not fulfilled their Virtue in a way that would grant a mortal Willpower, they must now <i>spend</i> a point of Willpower alongside the normal Vitae they spend to rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:24:31-08:00","id":807129,"title":"","content":"A bit harsh but definitely a great line of thought. What do you think about if they could pursue there Viture and choose to ignore it they loss a willpower. After all putting yourself in a bad situation every night does not allow for a long lived Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 01-12-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:45:44-08:00","id":818158,"title":"","content":"So put some more thinking into this a spoke with my group. So far we have the septemi have Auspex as their fourth discipline.<br /> Futher thinking of their devotions <br /> First one being <br /> <br /> Buttress the Soul <br /> <br /> With a word of prayer and a quick ritual of protection (usually the Passionate crosses herself), the Septemi can focus her supernatural defense against outside forces, heightening it for a brief moment. any harmful powers takes a penalty equal her rating in Majesty. The Buttress the Soul remains until the end of the sence. This power can be activated after an enemy declares that he will use a power against the Septemi but before the roll is resolved. Buttress the Soul involves some small ritual that can always be seen by onlookers but involves no blatantly supernatural display. Use of this power almost never constitutes a Masquerade violation, and only enemies with a strong knowledge of the Septemi will identify this power for what it is. <br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> Auspex 1 Majesty 1<br /> 2exp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T21:53:31-08:00","id":818986,"title":"","content":"I'd make it a merit with two mechanics. The first would be an always active passive effect that grants a bonus to any trait used to resist, contest, or withstand a supernatural effect equal to the merit dots. The second would be the ability to spend a willpower to make a Clash of Wills (Blood Potency + Merit Dots) to suppress an active supernatural power for an amount of time that raises with the dot rating, until finally at 5 dots you just permanently dispel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T22:09:16-08:00","id":818995,"title":"","content":"You know I rather like that, It seems very fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:06:48-08:00","id":819556,"title":"","content":"Cool. Well, to make it look a bit more like a merit:<br /> <br /> Abjurism (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Septemi<br /> Your character is trained in the ways of Abjurism, the techniques developed by the bloodline's founder for focusing the supernatural potency of the Blood. With it, you can not only better protect yourself against supernatural powers inflicted upon you by others, but extend your own will outward, suppressing or even dissipating existing magic.<br /> This merit provides two benefits, one passive and one active. The passive effect, often referred to as Buttressing the Soul, provides a bonus equal to the merit's rating to any dice pool your Septemi uses to contest a supernatural power targeting them. If there is no contested dice pool, it instead causes a penalty equal to the rating to the originator's activation pool, even if there's normally no resistance allowed. The benefit works against any type of power, from the Disciplines, Devotions, and Blood Magic of other Kindred, to the Arcana of Mages, the Numina of ephemeral entities, and anything else of a supernatural origin.<br /> The active benefit, sometimes referred to as Breaking the Weave, allows the Septemi to suppress supernatural powers (again, of any kind) that he's aware of for a length of time equal to that shown in the chart below, according to your rating in Abjurism. This requires that a willpower be spent, an instant action be taken, and a Clash of Wills made against the user or originator of the targeted effect, with Abjurism replacing the usual Discipline rating, and the maximum suppressed duration providing a bonus as if it were the effect's duration. If the Septemi wins the Clash of Wills, the effect is suppressed for the duration listed on the following chart, effectively disappearing for that period of time, its effects no longer working. If the effect's duration is equal to or lower than the maximum listed below, the effect is instead dissipated entirely, as if its duration suddenly ended. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Merit Dots</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Suppression Duration</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One turn per dot of Blood Potency</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One scene</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One chapter (or 1 day per dot of Blood Potency)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One story (or 1 month)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Permanent</td> </tr> </table></div> With two dots, the Possess manifestation can be ended using the same system. Three dots allows the Septemi to attempt to end a Fetter on a living being, ignoring the normal duration. Five dots can allow the Septemi to attempt to end the Claim condition on a living being, although this is treated as if the entity purposely detached itself, with the normal trouble for the host it causes. Similarly, five dots can potentially end a Stryx's Possess Living/Kindred/Revenant embodiments, although it won't affect Synthesis. All other manifestations and embodiments, including the listed ones against inanimate objects, use the normal systems for suppressing effects, although the Twilight Form manifestation and the Shadow Form embodiment cannot be suppressed, nor can similar 'default' capabilities.<br /> Abjurism cannot be used to disenchant supernatural objects, but it can target any effect generated by one. In the case of a singular &quot;always active&quot; effect generated by an object getting suppressed, the effect can be 'restarted' by the user by paying a point of willpower and using an instant action to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> EDIT: And to note, I do like the idea of them getting Auspex as their fourth discipline; it'd help them discover the effects they're working against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-02-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:39:45-08:00","id":819581,"title":"","content":"This looks great. I will definitely use this, it even caters to mage crossover issues. But what about the ability to remove the blood bond, would you say it takes a willpower dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 01-29-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:38:30-08:00","id":819643,"title":"","content":"I had been thinking about that, wasn't sure if I wanted to include that even as the fifth dot of a merit. I know there's already a Resilience threnody that can do it, but that's not exactly 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm kinda iffy on it, and would need to think it through, but if you wanted to include it, I'd say you need 3 dots to suppress it by one step for the listed duration, for a willpower point as normal, or 5 dots and a dot of willpower to permanently remove the full vinculum from someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:53:58-08:00","id":819648,"title":"","content":"I would say go with the original cost a willpower dot for the vampire and the bloodbonded character. Further the bloodbonded charcter must want to break free from his regnant in order to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:23:12-08:00","id":819805,"title":"","content":"Dot costs have been removed in 2ed so I wouldn't go with willpower dot costs personally.<br /> <br /> There aren't even experience costs to restore lost willpower dots anymore if I recall correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 01-30-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:43:31-08:00","id":819816,"title":"","content":"Using willpower dots are still a thing; mandate of the masses cost 1willpower dot, mages releasing their spells will cost 1willpower dot. Just to name a few thing that cost willpower dots, by the the cost to regain a spent willpower dot cost only 1 exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 01-30-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:16:00-08:00","id":819910,"title":"","content":"Yeah there are a few things, just far far less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:16:48-08:00","id":820800,"title":"","content":"Just realized that a bonus to withstand the Arcana of Mages would be a bit too much. As it was pointed out in the open dev that increasing the potency of a spell would -2 per potency therefore to get past the maximum from Abjurism they would need to take a -10, and well thats just needlessly punishing mages. So im thinking for mages the merits increases the Septemi withstand per 2 Dots, with the last Dot preventing mage from bypassing the vampires withstand rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:38:53-08:00","id":821177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=820800#post820800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just realized that a bonus to withstand the Arcana of Mages would be a bit too much. As it was pointed out in the open dev that increasing the potency of a spell would -2 per potency therefore to get past the maximum from Abjurism they would need to take a -10, and well thats just needlessly punishing mages. So im thinking for mages the merits increases the Septemi withstand per 2 Dots, with the last Dot preventing mage from bypassing the vampires withstand rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but remember if Potency is the primary factor (and it usually is) you automatically gain a bonus to it equal to your arcana rating. As it is, Mage's withstanding mechanic is way too potent versus other supernaturals as it is, in my view. But it's admittedly probably best to playtest it before figuring for sure if it's too potent or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-01-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:56:00-08:00","id":821445,"title":"","content":"Well vampires aren't lacking in boosting there resistant stats. They add there blood potency to the resistance when frenzied. But mages can when they get a exceptional success they can INGNORE the withstand raiting of everything being effected by the spell. So I would rather have three less to add to their withstand rating and have their withstand raiting not be able to be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 02-02-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:15:21-08:00","id":821631,"title":"","content":"Is there a post in the mage forum about how dispelling and counterspelling works in mage now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T09:09:26-08:00","id":821666,"title":"","content":"Counterspelling is a 1 level attainment for all Arcanum. Dave has mentioned to counterspell Werewolf's gifts would be spirit 2. Here is a link to the open dev.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-next-level-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-next-level-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Reaching the Next Level [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-next-level-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-next-level-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T09:18:59-08:00","id":821673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=821666#post821666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterspelling is a 1 level attainment for all Arcanum. Dave has mentioned to counterspell Werewolf's gifts would be spirit 2. Here is a link to the open dev.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-next-level-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/reaching-the-...the-awakening/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the practice of Shielding to defend from abilities that fall under the corresponding Arcana. Counterspelling is only usable against <i>spells</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-02-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:15:02-08:00","id":821708,"title":"","content":"I know the first Arcanum attainment is for spell only. but as mentioned by dave a spirit mage can counter a Werewolf's gift with a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439841#post439841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> (Well, okay, yes, but you'd need Life 7 to do it)<br /> <br /> Mages can't affect the internal powers of supernatural creatures. A spiit mage can attempt to Counterspell Gifts (which turns it into a Clash of Wills between werewolf and mage) but werewolves' regeneration, shapeshifting, spiritual senses, honorary rank, ability to Reach and so on are untouchable except for archmages,</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656969#post656969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acceleration? No, it's Time 3 spell.<br /> <br /> If the mage knows she's fighting werewolves and has Spirit 2, she can Clash of Wills whenever someone uses a Gift on her, as well.<br /> <br /> Now, if the mage in our increasingly-unlikely scenario is a <i>master</i> (of any Arcanum)... Well... That's like the aggravated-damage adept scenario only more so. Instead of doing levels of damage, a master can Unmake or Make her Arcanum in the subject's pattern in fatal ways - if it's a Forces mage you're after, we'll say Unmaking Forces to remove all electrical activity from the poor sob that pissed off someone who lists &quot;mastery of the universes' fundamental energies&quot; on her resume.<br /> <br /> Unlike doing health boxes of damage, this one's actually withstood. Her Potency will be reduced, assuming she casts successfully to start with, by the subject's Stamina. If she has <i>any</i> successes left, the subject dies. Instantly. No matter how much health he has. Her Potency <i>starts</i> at 5, so she would instantly slay all but Olympic athletes, but we'll be generous and assume the person fighting her knows what she is so is going to spend willpower and raise his passive resistance to, say, 6 (assuming he had stamina 4). That's still only -2 dice, though, against a character who has a base dice pool of <i>at least</i> 10, and will probably be spending willpower herself on top of whatever the one yantra she's allowed in a single-turn spell uses. The Paradox will be about the same as the adept, but her foes' chance of survival is a lot slimmer. As with all passive resistances, Withstood spells do not give you more resistance for having a Supernatural Tolerance Trait. All that matters is your Stamina, give or take a +2 for burning Willpower.<br /> <br /> As before, however, if the werewolf's in war form he's probably got a superhuman Stamina, and like the adept she'll be bleeding dice to account for his massive size. If so, and the master casts her death spell but didn't build a potency high enough... Nothing happens. And then the werewolf kills her.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:25:51-08:00","id":821714,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected. That's... hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-02-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:16:28-08:00","id":821744,"title":"","content":"A vampire should technically be able to use vitae to up Stamina if it's targeted by a withstood spell too, if aware of the attempt somehow. But that's irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think it's silly that you don't withstand damage spells because they already are accounted for in health levels. But really, the withstanding mechanics in general are one of the few things I heavily dislike about new mage. Again, I disgress though, the important note there is it also makes abjurism useless there as written for damaging spells.<br /> <br /> Maybe it should be changed to be add dice to contested rolls only, and for anything else you simply subtract dice, even if not normally resistable? That would affect mage spells like anything else; even if it wouldn't be quite as potent, it'd always work, at least, and also adds the benefit for working on certain Demon powers that don't have proper resistance, too. WHat do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:54:49-08:00","id":822040,"title":"","content":"Vitae to up Stamina is a thing it one of the ways to defend from magic. Having it be a penalty to all magical effects works more closely to the original. Also the withstand of magic works kind of like armor it reduces how well the spell effects you if at all and I do agree with you damaging spell not being effected by withstand is total shit. But they do still have to hit there target for the spell effect a vampire or werewolf could get the hell out of dodge very easily with vampire having celerity to move out of range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T19:13:36-08:00","id":822053,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've changed the wording.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that's true, unless the mage used Reach to make it sensory range, or another reach to make it sympathetic in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T19:24:13-08:00","id":822060,"title":"","content":"At sensory range still needs to hit them. They literally throw the spell at them at that point which the vampire and werewolf could still dodge. As for sympathetic connection has its own withstand rating, not sure how much it would be but it still some defense. While a arrow may be to shoot spells like guns their are wsys to avoid it, Hell there is CQQ fighting merit that at first level lets double more away from a ranged attack at the price of there next insist action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28