e":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T12:18:31-08:00","id":825052,"title":"","content":"Recently came across some information that supernal damage does apply to armor if it makes sense. So how about Buttress of the Soul act as magical armor vs damaging effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:46:25-08:00","id":825693,"title":"","content":"That seems to bring it to the same issue as adding it straight to withstanding, namely the amount of power it provides, and also a little overcomplicating. I think at this point that's not really needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T19:08:24-08:00","id":825703,"title":"","content":"Hmm thats is true. So how about multiple merits for different benefit, one centering around prevention and the other around countering? That way its not too much of a benefit for 5 exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T23:26:49-07:00","id":849622,"title":"","content":"I have finished my update of the Septemi Bloodline. There is a Google Doc in the original post but I will post another link here as well.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cvuaopl5laSlndKj4cgIl1j9q9PyMsGTYdnGNo4qvBc/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...p=docslist_api</a><br /> <br /> I would like to thank everyone who gave a hand in the update of this bloodline. And I would like to not that I decided to return to devotions for the basses of its powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 03-19-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:45:03-07:00","id":849709,"title":"","content":"My thoughts as I read this that you are free to ignore:<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane - It is unclear to me as to whether they can buff Stamina to the full amount (+2 per Vitae) or not at all. This also feels tremendously weak--as in, not enough of a bane to matter. In 1e, I saw a lot of blood buffing because one shotting people was a real possibility, so, blood spent on offense was valuable. But in 2e, with Defense getting high enough to actually matter, and more importantly, weapons dealing bashing instead of lethal, fights last longer and healing 2 bashing for 1 blood is a way more valuable use than adding 2 to hit. And in neither edition have I ever seen blood spent on physical intensity outside of combat.<br /> <br /> Their old flaw was about following Virtue (in addition to the normal Daeva following Vice). Since Daeva are now &quot;promiscuous feeders,&quot; it's probably harder to directly parallel that. I don't know, I'll think about options, but this blood buff nerf just feels like it doesn't matter at all.<br /> <br /> Abjurism is excellent. I see now that mentioning Stamina was irrelevant in the flaw.<br /> <br /> Buttress the Soul is tricky. First, it requires you to take actual, physical action, so, there's a little disconnect for me when it comes to powers that have no obvious physical manifestation. Abjurism is more like an insinctual thing--you feel it affecting you and you can just reflexively defend. But this, you feel it affecting you and in that moment, you can do the sign of the cross? That's...odd. Not bad, just odd.<br /> <br /> It also gets muddy at the end when you're talking about Withstand and all that. So, right off the bat, I don't know new Mage at all--my love of Ascension just never let me move on to Awakening--but I read this thread and from their description, I don't really think your addition is necessary at all. Don't Mages still have to roll to cast a spell that uses &quot;withstand&quot; instead of resistance? You mentioned something about a -2 per Potency or something. So, you're basically double dipping here. They already take a penalty equal to your Majesty to the roll anyway. Why add another penalty equal to their Majesty (effectively) by raising your Withstand? Can't you just use Abjurism to boost your withstand by raising the appropriate resist attribute (which seems worded specifically to allow that, unlike blood buff, which doesn't raise the actual attribute, just die pools tied to it). Also, since you can reflexively do the sign of the cross or whatever ritual you choose consider making it a Majesty/Celerity devotion.<br /> <br /> Ok, so, can a Septemi not really effectively use Buttress the Soul unless they have The Light of Truth on? Is the thing about receiving visions a side benefit you left purposefully vague, or is it the fluffy description of how they keep half their defense (awkward, by the way, I don't think it would be overpowered to keep the whole defense) and notice supernatural powers targeting them? You might want to consider an Auspex/Celerity requirement, rather than just Auspex.<br /> <br /> Breaking the Wave feels like it should cost Willpower, either in addition to, or instead of the Vitae. It also is very unclear as to the die pool of your clash of wills. Normally, you roll Discipline + Blood Potency...since this is a Vigor devotion, does that mean you use Vigor + Blood Potency? For a bloodline focused on defense to the degree that they can't bloodbuff Strength to its fullest, Vigor seems inappropriate to invest in. Majesty and/or Auspex seem most appropriate here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-19-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:30:30-07:00","id":849927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=849709#post849709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts as I read this that you are free to ignore:<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane - It is unclear to me as to whether they can buff Stamina to the full amount (+2 per Vitae) or not at all. This also feels tremendously weak--as in, not enough of a bane to matter. In 1e, I saw a lot of blood buffing because one shotting people was a real possibility, so, blood spent on offense was valuable. But in 2e, with Defense getting high enough to actually matter, and more importantly, weapons dealing bashing instead of lethal, fights last longer and healing 2 bashing for 1 blood is a way more valuable use than adding 2 to hit. And in neither edition have I ever seen blood spent on physical intensity outside of combat.<br /> <br /> Their old flaw was about following Virtue (in addition to the normal Daeva following Vice). Since Daeva are now &quot;promiscuous feeders,&quot; it's probably harder to directly parallel that. I don't know, I'll think about options, but this blood buff nerf just feels like it doesn't matter at all.<br /> <br /> Abjurism is excellent. I see now that mentioning Stamina was irrelevant in the flaw.<br /> <br /> Buttress the Soul is tricky. First, it requires you to take actual, physical action, so, there's a little disconnect for me when it comes to powers that have no obvious physical manifestation. Abjurism is more like an insinctual thing--you feel it affecting you and you can just reflexively defend. But this, you feel it affecting you and in that moment, you can do the sign of the cross? That's...odd. Not bad, just odd.<br /> <br /> It also gets muddy at the end when you're talking about Withstand and all that. So, right off the bat, I don't know new Mage at all--my love of Ascension just never let me move on to Awakening--but I read this thread and from their description, I don't really think your addition is necessary at all. Don't Mages still have to roll to cast a spell that uses &quot;withstand&quot; instead of resistance? You mentioned something about a -2 per Potency or something. So, you're basically double dipping here. They already take a penalty equal to your Majesty to the roll anyway. Why add another penalty equal to their Majesty (effectively) by raising your Withstand? Can't you just use Abjurism to boost your withstand by raising the appropriate resist attribute (which seems worded specifically to allow that, unlike blood buff, which doesn't raise the actual attribute, just die pools tied to it). Also, since you can reflexively do the sign of the cross or whatever ritual you choose consider making it a Majesty/Celerity devotion.<br /> <br /> Ok, so, can a Septemi not really effectively use Buttress the Soul unless they have The Light of Truth on? Is the thing about receiving visions a side benefit you left purposefully vague, or is it the fluffy description of how they keep half their defense (awkward, by the way, I don't think it would be overpowered to keep the whole defense) and notice supernatural powers targeting them? You might want to consider an Auspex/Celerity requirement, rather than just Auspex.<br /> <br /> Breaking the Wave feels like it should cost Willpower, either in addition to, or instead of the Vitae. It also is very unclear as to the die pool of your clash of wills. Normally, you roll Discipline + Blood Potency...since this is a Vigor devotion, does that mean you use Vigor + Blood Potency? For a bloodline focused on defense to the degree that they can't bloodbuff Strength to its fullest, Vigor seems inappropriate to invest in. Majesty and/or Auspex seem most appropriate here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for your input, I honesty love when people give their thoughts and ideas it allows me to fix mistakes or vague things.<br /> <br /> What sort of Bloodline Bane would you recommend to be then? I honesty don't like the one I have so far, but I feel that giving them a Virtue doesn't quite work ether. So if you have an idea im all ears.<br /> <br /> Buttress of the Soul is supports to be used once to activate the effect, then the vampire gets the benefits of the devotion for the rest of the scene. So he only brings up the cross once.<br /> <br /> The point of Light of Truth is to gives a heads up of hostile attacks or effects that could harm the vampire. So yes the seeing vision is the fluff of the devotion. Its actual meant to allow the vampire know when to use Abjurism to defend themselves. Also changed it back to 1 Celerity 1 Auspex.<br /> <br /> As for Breaking the Weave I added in what to roll, which by the way is Vigor + Blood Potency. The reason I have it Vigor is a few reasons, such as encouraging the vampire to actually get Vigor despite the fact that physical intensity is weakened for the use of strength. The other reason its Vigor is its using spiritual strength the destroy the opposing supernatural effect, sense Vigor is the discipline of strength it felt the most fitting.<br /> <br /> Lastly for Abjurism is worded exactly the same way as Physical Intensity in 2E. Which by the way actually can be used to raise their withstand raiting. The major difference between the Abjurism and Buttress of the Soul is that Buttress is used once to gain its benefits while Abjurism must be used every turn they are effected by a supernatural effect. So buttress is more cost effective while Abjurism can give higher short burts of protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 03-19-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:56:17-07:00","id":850140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=849927#post849927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of Bloodline Bane would you recommend to be then? I honesty don't like the one I have so far, but I feel that giving them a Virtue doesn't quite work ether. So if you have an idea im all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, exactly. The theme of the clan seems to be a middle finger to the Sanctum--Christianity applies equally to humans and vampires. And they're obviously very protective/defensive focused. There's a lot of thematic space to play in, but the mechanical side has much less room.<br /> <br /> Brief, half formed ideas that are not sufficient without refinement in rapid succession:<br /> -Maybe play with the guilty condition somehow--they feel guilty when...doing bad stuff is too vague.<br /> -Maybe add some of the old Humanity chart back? So, they actually lose Humanity for sinning, as in, the Christianity stuff, rather than just being inhuman? Probably too cumbersome, though.<br /> -Adjust the Humanity chart? Maybe they're considered to be 1 or 2 Humanity higher on the chart for what they consider to be breaking points? This might work, actually...<br /> -Maybe something with Lashing Out? Perhaps they have to spend a willpower to use it on a person? That's probably not severe enough, but maybe as a secondary part of the flaw<br /> -Get the Guilty condition when you inflict a condition on a mortal using a supernatural power (like, Majesty to enslave, or lashing out to make them Wanton)<br /> -Give the Guilty condition when facing a breaking point, regardless of result?<br /> -A penalty to using supernatural powers against mortals? Based on Humanity? Or Blood Potency?<br /> -Maybe adjust the dependency part of the Daeva bane. They can get dependent after one drink (so, they stick to animals)? Or they get a lesser condition that forms a 1 step bond after one drink (and still the 2 step after 2)?<br /> -Something will Willpower? Maybe, they can't spend a Willpower to get +3 to cause harm to someone? Or maybe just not to harm a mortal, including mindraping them with Dominate/Majesty?<br /> <br /> I don't know, I'll think more about it, too, but it's a hard flaw to translate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=849927#post849927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of Light of Truth is to gives a heads up of hostile attacks or effects that could harm the vampire. So yes the seeing vision is the fluff of the devotion. Its actual meant to allow the vampire know when to use Abjurism to defend themselves. Also changed it back to 1 Celerity 1 Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, wait, you can't spend blood to get +2 to defend against a power unless you know it's coming, but you can cross yourself and drop their pool by Majesty?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=849927#post849927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Breaking the Weave I added in what to roll, which by the way is Vigor + Blood Potency. The reason I have it Vigor is a few reasons, such as encouraging the vampire to actually get Vigor despite the fact that physical intensity is weakened for the use of strength. The other reason its Vigor is its using spiritual strength the destroy the opposing supernatural effect, sense Vigor is the discipline of strength it felt the most fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think Majesty, the strength of your aura or whatever, is more appropriate than physical strength, but that's just personal taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:08:14-07:00","id":850172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=850140#post850140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Maybe something with Lashing Out? Perhaps they have to spend a willpower to use it on a person? That's probably not severe enough, but maybe as a secondary part of the flaw<br /> -Get the Guilty condition when you inflict a condition on a mortal using a supernatural power (like, Majesty to enslave, or lashing out to make them Wanton)</div> </div> </div> </div>actually being forced to spend a willpower to lash out on a human is very cool and in theme. Along with gaining the guilty condition when you inflict an condition on humans. Its seems to be just as punishing as the other 2E bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=850140#post850140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, wait, you can't spend blood to get +2 to defend against a power unless you know it's coming, but you can cross yourself and drop their pool by Majesty?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that im trying to convey is that Buttress of the Soul is more like an passive protection, much like Mage Armor. It's paid once and last for the scene. They don't bring up the cross on every supernatural effect that attacks them, its supposed to be something that dampens the incoming effect.<br /> Maybe I sould put some more fluff in it describing the use of your force of personality weakens incoming harmful effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=850140#post850140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think Majesty, the strength of your aura or whatever, is more appropriate than physical strength, but that's just personal taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I see your point I just don't want to center a second ability on Majesty. If I do so it would encourage people to power through Majesty to gain major benefits. While if I keep it Vigor then the player would be tempted to go into ether power, and it would slow them down because they would have to spend more exp to max out both devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T22:31:32-07:00","id":851594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=850140#post850140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Maybe something with Lashing Out? Perhaps they have to spend a willpower to use it on a person? That's probably not severe enough, but maybe as a secondary part of the flaw<br /> -Get the Guilty condition when you inflict a condition on a mortal using a supernatural power (like, Majesty to enslave, or lashing out to make them Wanton)</div> </div> </div> </div>I got a new Bane up it play off the fact the Septemi Needs to act for the greater good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:12:50-07:00","id":851695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=851594#post851594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a new Bane up it play off the fact the Septemi Needs to act for the greater good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's harsh. A penalty for having below 8? So, you have to <i>raise</i> Humanity just to not get a penalty? I think you might be better off just rolling Humanity straight out like the Daeva, rather than rolling Res+Comp - (8-Humanity).<br /> <br /> I think you're in for some arguments at the table with this one. The &quot;greater good&quot; is too ill defined, way too open for debate. You might get someone, for example, who believes in social darwinism, so, they won't feed the poor because letting them die off is for the greater good. It's too vague, I think, is the problem. A least in the old system, someone had a previously defined virtue to uphold. Now, they have sort of open reign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T09:26:13-07:00","id":851821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=851695#post851695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that's harsh. A penalty for having below 8? So, you have to <i>raise</i> Humanity just to not get a penalty? I think you might be better off just rolling Humanity straight out like the Daeva, rather than rolling Res+Comp - (8-Humanity).<br /> <br /> I think you're in for some arguments at the table with this one. The &quot;greater good&quot; is too ill defined, way too open for debate. You might get someone, for example, who believes in social darwinism, so, they won't feed the poor because letting them die off is for the greater good. It's too vague, I think, is the problem. A least in the old system, someone had a previously defined virtue to uphold. Now, they have sort of open reign.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of rolling just your humanity never accrued to me. Fuck I feel like an idiot. And I agree about the Greater Good its to vague but I don't want to make it narrow. Well ether way I reworked it.<br /> Bloodline Bane: Septemi are far from being heroes, their blood addicts them to the rush of martyrdom, the pleasure inherent in giving of themselves for an apparent greater good. Every maiden is a believer, while they all may not believe in the same thing each hold a ideal or faith close to their heart. All Passionate\u2019s gain the Virtue Faith as Persistent Addicted Condition. Resisting an opportunity to commit an altruistic act for her Faith requires a roll Humanity. Failure results in the Persistent Addicted Deprived Condition.<br /> <br /> And once again thanks for your imput.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:34:28-07:00","id":851893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=851821#post851821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodline Bane: Septemi are far from being heroes, their blood addicts them to the rush of martyrdom, the pleasure inherent in giving of themselves for an apparent greater good. Every maiden is a believer, while they all may not believe in the same thing each hold a ideal or faith close to their heart. All Passionate\u2019s gain the Virtue Faith as Persistent Addicted Condition. Resisting an opportunity to commit an altruistic act for her Faith requires a roll Humanity. Failure results in the Persistent Addicted Deprived Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are we talking about Faith, like 1e faith, where it's about finding purpose in chaos, or do you mean something else? Because 2e virtues are self-defined. I think the current form works <i>at your table</i> where you can explain what you mean by Faith, but if meant for general consumption, it's still a huge grey area. Can I have Faith that I'm the most awesome badass vampire in the world? Can I be a &quot;jihadist?&quot; Satanist? A follower of Cthulhu? The Flying Spaghetti Monster?<br /> <br /> You clearly have some idea in mind of what &quot;altruistic acts for her Faith&quot; are, but it's very difficult to get that across to others in a short paragraph, rather than a conversation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T19:55:32-07:00","id":852201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/806850-how-to-update-the-septemi-bloodline?p=851893#post851893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can I be a &amp;quot;jihadist?&amp;quot; Satanist? A follower of Cthulhu? The Flying Spaghetti Monster?<br /> <br /> You clearly have some idea in mind of what &amp;quot;altruistic acts for her Faith&amp;quot; are, but it's very difficult to get that across to others in a short paragraph, rather than a conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your right, im trying to convey that the Septemi take up an ideal cause. Be it religious or a progressive movement, im also trying to give a systematic reason for their radical almost terrorist ways of helping those causes.<br /> I want them to believe in something bigger then themselves not other vampires would never put thought to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}